  <p class="lead">
    Relocating to the United Kingdom as a foreign worker, managing overseas assets while resident in the UK, or living abroad as a UK expat involves navigating a maze of complex international tax regulations. <strong>HM Revenue & Customs (HMRC)</strong> enforces strict global tax reporting, while international double tax treaties determine which country holds primary taxing rights. The landscape shifted dramatically with the introduction of the 2025/2026 tax reforms, making older advice obsolete.
  </p>
  <p>
